  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Oceanographic Survey of the East-China Sea",
  "description": "Oceanographic surveys have been conducted at 175 stations (22 lines) in the East China Sea since 1995. Data collected 4 times a year include fish larvae and eggs, temperature, salinity, DO, zooplankton, nutrients, Chl-a, and currents. Data obtained from the surveys have been published as \"Annual report of oceanographic observations\" and are available through the Korean Oceanographic Data Center (KODC). [ Reference: PICES Scientific Report No. 18 2001, Proceedings of the PICES/CoML/IPRC Workshop on \"Impact of Climate Variability on Observation and Prediction of Ecosystem and Biodiversity Changes in the North Pacific\", http://www.pices.int/publications/scientific_reports/Report18/default.aspx. ]\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To extend and evaluate potential fishing grounds and to access marine environmental quality.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23516098",
